> Tests are failing on Helix at `Assert.True(File.Exists(fileName));` - @MattGal @HaoK these tests are testing the File Logger I added in this PR, which, in the tests, is writing to `Path.GetTempFileName()`. Would that behavior be different on Helix?

@wtgodbe the only thing we do is to create a per-Helix-job temp folder and set this to the value of TEMP and TMP in the environment of a Helix work item.  In the logs you linked, the process' TEMP would be an (already existent) `/datadisks/disk1/work/A0CF08F2/t`   .  As the same API is used in dozens of runtime tests including the tests for [the API itself](https://github.com/dotnet/runtime/blob/01b7e73cd378145264a7cb7a09365b41ed42b240/src/libraries/System.Runtime.Extensions/tests/System/IO/PathTests.cs#L178) I am skeptical that helix execution is causing this.  

I'll dig a bit more and see if I find anything interesting.

